{"name":"Scallion","hex":"#6b8e23","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Scallion","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname from Irish."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Scallion"}],"entries":[{"title":"Scallion","blocks":[{"text":"Scallions are edible vegetables of various species in the genus Allium. Scallions generally have a milder taste than most onions. Green onions/scallions have a long, delicate green stem that is white near the root. They have no bulb and a mild, sweet onion flavour. Their close relatives include garlic, shallots, leeks, chives, and Chinese onions. The leaves are eaten both raw and cooked."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/CSA-Red-Spring-Onions.jpg/330px-CSA-Red-Spring-Onions.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scallion"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Germinating_scallion.jpg/500px-Germinating_scallion.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Germinating_scallion.jpg/500px-Germinating_scallion.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A germinating scallion, 10 days old","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGerminating_scallion.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/2010-06-19-supermarkt-by-RalfR-32.jpg/500px-2010-06-19-supermarkt-by-RalfR-32.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/2010-06-19-supermarkt-by-RalfR-32.jpg/1280px-2010-06-19-supermarkt-by-RalfR-32.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/2010-06-19-supermarkt-by-RalfR-32.jpg/500px-2010-06-19-sup